# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# me: Pronoun. "(personal) inflection of yo (accusative): me"
# te: Pronoun. "inflection of tú,vos (dative): to you, for you"
# lo: Pronoun. "inflection of él (acc) and usted (when referring to a man), and a variant of ello in many constructions; hi..."
# la: Pronoun. "inflection of ella (acc), ello (when the antecedent's implied gender is feminine), and usted (when referrin..."
# le: Pronoun. "to him, for him; inflection of él (dat)"
# nos: Pronoun. "inflection of nosotros (dative): to us, for us"
# os: Pronoun. "dative and accusative of vosotros: you, to you, for you"
# les: Pronoun. "inflection of ellos,ellas (dative); to them, for them"
# se: Pronoun. "A reflexive or reciprocal pronoun: oneself, himself, herself, itself, yourself; themselves; yourselves; eac..."
me
te
lo
la
le
nos
os
les
se
